## Notifications and activity

Ordinary widgets can use `HostServices.Notifications` with bounded manifest
`notificationCategories`. Introduce optional categories during setup and call
`ConfigureAsync(categoryId)` from an action to open shared host preferences. Do
not store a duplicate enabled/opacity choice. Use `UpdateAsync` for metadata or
progress without replaying a banner, and a declared `OpenIntent` for a pending
result destination. `SourceHidden` lets the host suppress redundant results when
the owner is already visible. Notifications do not extend worker lifetime.

Report independent `HostServices.Activity.SetAsync(sourceId, activity)` sources
only for activity the widget owns; clearing one source leaves the others intact.
WebView audio and website notifications are detected by the host automatically;
webapp wrappers need no DOM polling or mirrored status reporting. Website notices
use the General category and their original website activation callback, with
banners eligible whether the overlay is open or hidden. Ordinary SDK notices
default to OverlayHidden; set `Visibility = WidgetNotificationVisibility.Always`
when they should also appear while the overlay is open.

Keep stable focus IDs and declare navigation/Back destinations. The host preserves
widget focus through snapshot replacement; notification publication must not
change the widget's route or force focus.

Declare a notification category's `retention` as `bannerOnly` for transient notices
or `pending` for notices kept in the list. The host enforces this declaration and
shows useful controls: On/Off for banner-only categories, or Banner + list / List
only / Off for pending categories. Omitting `retention` allows both kinds for
existing categories. Do not advertise pending-list choices for song banners.
